                    briefing_text_r2:       `Your instinct is to cut prices to match MegaBuild's 8–15% lower commodity prices. But a <strong>blanket 10% cut</strong> on the ~60% commodity volume erases roughly <em>$130k of gross profit</em> — more than half of owner cash flow — for a price war you cannot win. The discipline: match price only on ~10 visible <strong>known-value SKUs</strong> to protect your price image cheaply, hold the line everywhere else, and <strong>add value</strong> (delivery, expertise) on service items rather than discount them.`,
